Z||000014||Blacktree||12-28-2001||02:56 AM||||Yup, pay to play as they say.<P>I tried out WinMX, and it's not too bad. It just irks me when I download a file, find out it sucks (bad quality), decide to download it from someone else... and everyone else has that very same crappy-quality MP3. You'd think SOMEONE would have the sense to encode or find a better-quality version of the file, instead of spreading the crappy one all over WinMX. <P>The peeps on WinMX need to be introduced to VBR encoding.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Nashco||12-28-2001||04:29 AM||||I've tried almost all of the above programs, and I'm still true to Morpheus.  There's never been anything I <B>couldn't</B> find on Morpheus, from stuff I've never heard before to the latest "please stop playing that frickin' song" stuff.<P>I liked AudioGalaxy quite a bit, but was unhappy with the amount of information available for the download BEFORE I downloaded it.  My roommate has Bear Share (sp?) and he liked it a lot, almost exactly the same as Morpheus apparently, but I never downloaded it...if it's the same what would be the point? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Try Morpheus, it's got everything I've wanted so far except for one very minor detail...you can't initiate a chat with some people in certain circumstances, but most people don't do that anyway.  Have fun!<P>------------------<BR>Bryce<BR> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/nashcosig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fleabitdog||12-28-2001||07:35 AM||||I like Morpheus myself, besides mp3's I got Adobe 6.0(full) M/Soft frontpage (full) Return to castle wolfenstein and can find just about anything else I want. All for free. Only thing I don't like about it is I have to figure out how to get it to shut down completely w/o doing a cntrl/alt/del. Small price to pay.  Dave||||reg||1
Z||000017||8Ball||12-28-2001||07:41 AM||||Have you any details as to what exactly your computer is doing. I.E. not completeing d/l's?<BR>What have you installed lately, hardward and software.<BR>Any error messages?<BR>What OS are you running?<BR>How much free space on your HD?<BR>And last but not least, (sorry I have to ask this) Are you SURE you not telling it to save to the a: drive?<BR>E.B.||||reg||1
Z||000018||fropuff||12-28-2001||10:17 AM||||Have you any details as to what exactly your computer is doing. I.E. not completeing d/l's?<BR>-Well, when I was doing Morpheus, which is a 1.6 MB download, it went to 1.44 MB, and stopped like it was done.  Then on Napigator, which is a 2.41 MB program, it went up to 1.9 MB and stopped like it was done.  Then when I went to click on it, it said that it did not complete downloading and for me to install it again.  I did it again, and the same thing happened.  <P>What have you installed lately, hardward and software.<BR>-I just finished installing the CD drive in Drive E, as well as taking out and re-installing the CD-Rom drive in Drive D.  Both seem to work just fine, and I'm not having any problems any longer.<P>Any error messages?<BR>-No, there aren't any error messages when downloading.<P>What OS are you running?<BR>-??? (consider me a computer retard.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>How much free space on your HD?<BR>-I have 8.52 GB free space on Drive C, which I'm saving the program to.  <P>And last but not least, (sorry I have to ask this) Are you SURE you not telling it to save to the a: drive?<BR>- <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Yes, I'm saving it to Drive C on the desktop<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||72vinman||12-28-2001||10:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fleabitdog:<BR><B>I like Morpheus myself, Only thing I don't like about it is I have to figure out how to get it to shut down completely w/o doing a cntrl/alt/del. Small price to pay.  Dave</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When you are in the Morpheus program window and you close the program it sends the program to the desktop tray in the right corner of your screen. Right mouse click on the Morpheus icon, a samll menu will appear. Then click on "Close Morpheus".<BR>I hope this helps.<BR>Vince<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigvin2_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||TRiAD||12-28-2001||10:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fropuff:<BR><B>...What OS are you running?<BR>-??? (consider me a computer retard.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think he said he was running WIN98<P><B> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>...And last but not least, (sorry I have to ask this) Are you SURE you not telling it to save to the a: drive?<BR>-  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Yes, I'm saving it to Drive C on the desktop.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Could this be the problem? When it tells you where it's going to save by default, it sounds like you're re-routing it to the link on your desktop. Your desktop is fine for holding shortcuts, but I think there's a built-in limit in 98 for how much you can put there. If you're actually storing the program on the desktop, that could be the problem. Try storing it in "My Computer/Local Drive C:/[program name]". <P>Hope this helps!<BR>||||reg||1
